       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day):** the maximum dose, often used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily:** a more typical range for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day, split into doses:** this may be what was meant if the 1600 mg was a daily total.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. It would probably be worth confirming with pharmacy first."
